  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689758",
      "title": "Element Transitions",
      "lectureOrder": 131,
      "videoOrder": 115,
      "sourceHash": "326be5b4dd05a87bbbf51f246dd7b81020aaf598bba23f14b1158bdaace77af4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.26,
          "end": 3.76,
          "en": "To animate in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.45,
          "end": 10.36,
          "en": "Such items, we can tap into the built in transitions Svelte offers us now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.39,
          "end": 16.24,
          "en": "Transitions differ from motions because motions are essentially animated values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 16.27,
          "end": 21.97,
          "en": "Transitions allow us to animate the appearance and disappearance of elements so elements rendered in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.97,
          "end": 22.66,
          "en": "the Dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.99,
          "end": 25.21,
          "en": "For that we import from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.12,
          "end": 27.11,
          "en": "Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.77,
          "end": 29.06,
          "en": "Transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.33,
          "end": 34.45,
          "en": "And from there we got four different transitions we can import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.48,
          "end": 39.42,
          "en": "We got fade, we got fly, we got slide and we got scale.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.43,
          "end": 40.87,
          "en": "We'll have a look at all of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.11,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "Now how do we apply a transition?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.21,
          "end": 48.67,
          "en": "We simply go to the element which will eventually appear or disappear, in our case, our div here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.76,
          "end": 55.03,
          "en": "And then we simply add transition colon and then for example, fade.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.03,
          "end": 58.48,
          "en": "So the name of the transition we want to use, you have to import that first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.48,
          "end": 61.39,
          "en": "So first of all, import fade from svelte transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.39,
          "end": 65.02,
          "en": "Thereafter, with the help of the transition directive, you can attach it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "Now, if you do that, let's try this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "Let's add apples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.62,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "And now you see that this fades in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.51,
          "end": 75.6,
          "en": "Let's do the same for bananas.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 76.89,
          "en": "And this fades in as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.89,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "And the same for oranges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.28999999999999,
          "end": 81.25,
          "en": "It fades in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.78999999999999,
          "end": 84.01,
          "en": "Now fade is just one transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.01,
          "end": 85.99,
          "en": "We can also give scale a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.99,
          "end": 88.57,
          "en": "And for that, of course, you need to import scale.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.47,
          "end": 93.22,
          "en": "If you do this and again I add my.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.86,
          "end": 94.94,
          "en": "Apple's here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.12,
          "end": 102.2,
          "en": "Now, you see this is coming in really small and then gets bigger and bigger until it reaches its full",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.5,
          "end": 103.34,
          "en": "size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.34,
          "end": 106.89,
          "en": "We also got slide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.92,
          "end": 109.7,
          "en": "So let's try out slide here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "Slide Also, just as all the other transitions needs to be imported and with slide added down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "we get a nice sliding effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.4,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "Here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "You see it roll down from the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 123.69,
          "en": "Like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.3,
          "end": 127.01,
          "en": "Now, last but not least, we got fly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.03,
          "end": 132.07,
          "en": "And now if I add fly like this and of course you have to import that as well, it should fly in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.07,
          "end": 138.85,
          "en": "But actually you will see that as I add my apples, it just fades in and that happens because you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.85,
          "end": 144.25,
          "en": "also pass some parameters to these transitions and some transitions work really fine out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.25,
          "end": 145.96,
          "en": "without any special parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.99,
          "end": 147.67000000000002,
          "en": "Others need parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.7,
          "end": 153.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now you add parameters simply by adding a equals sign here, and then your single curly braces to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.57999999999998,
          "end": 154.72,
          "en": "a dynamic value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.72,
          "end": 158.17000000000002,
          "en": "And now the dynamic value is a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.17000000000002,
          "end": 160.15,
          "en": "So another pair of curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.15,
          "end": 163.27,
          "en": "But this is not a double curly brace syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.27,
          "end": 169.3,
          "en": "Instead, it's still a single curly brace that tells Svelte that we're about to add a dynamically calculated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.3,
          "end": 169.9,
          "en": "value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.9,
          "end": 175.39,
          "en": "But then the dynamically calculated value or the JavaScript expression, to be precise, is simply a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.39,
          "end": 177.16,
          "en": "single JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.28,
          "end": 181.06,
          "en": "Now, in that object, you can pass key value pairs to configure that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.15,
          "end": 183.4,
          "en": "Now all transitions have a delay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.4,
          "end": 189.35,
          "en": "Property where you can define how long it should wait before it starts animating and a duration property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.35,
          "end": 192.56,
          "en": "in milliseconds where you can define how long it should take.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.59,
          "end": 197.51,
          "en": "The default is 400 and that is the case for all four transitions I showed you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.87,
          "end": 199.34,
          "en": "Now all transitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.34,
          "end": 206.6,
          "en": "But the fade transition also have an easing property where you can assign one of these easing functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 206.6,
          "end": 208.76,
          "en": "which you have to import from svelte easing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 208.76,
          "end": 214.7,
          "en": "So you can then add something like cubic in if you wanted to and then scale and fly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.7,
          "end": 217.04,
          "en": "Also got some other extra properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 217.37,
          "end": 225.8,
          "en": "Scale also got a start and an opacity property where start is simply the start size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 225.8,
          "end": 229.28,
          "en": "The default is zero, but you could start at half size for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.73,
          "end": 233.21,
          "en": "And opacity is the starting opacity here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.21,
          "end": 237.77,
          "en": "The default is also zero so that it also fades in whilst also being scaled in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.77,
          "end": 242.48,
          "en": "But here you could also start at full opacity or half opacity or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 242.78,
          "end": 252.17,
          "en": "Now fly also has more than just delay, duration and easing because fly also in addition has opacity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.17,
          "end": 255.11,
          "en": "because it also starts at zero opacity as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 255.11,
          "end": 256.34,
          "en": "But you can change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 256.34,
          "end": 263.21,
          "en": "And in addition it also has X and Y, which defines the x and y offset with which it starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.21,
          "end": 268.01,
          "en": "And the default here is zero, which is why we actually see no fly in effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 268.01,
          "end": 269.86,
          "en": "But you can change that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 269.87,
          "end": 275.99,
          "en": "You can, for example, set X to 300 and now see how that changes the fly animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 275.99,
          "end": 282.08,
          "en": "If I now add apples here, you see it fly in from the bottom and you see that it starts really slow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 282.08,
          "end": 285.74,
          "en": "and ends faster because I added the cubic in easing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 285.74,
          "end": 292.22,
          "en": "If I remove cubic in, then you'll see a linear easing here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 293.40999999999997,
          "end": 298.87,
          "en": "If you add -300, it will slide in or fly in from the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 298.87,
          "end": 302.02,
          "en": "So now if I add apples like this, it comes in from the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 302.02,
          "end": 306.91,
          "en": "And you can also, of course, add an X value like 200.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 306.91,
          "end": 309.04,
          "en": "So now I have both X and Y.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 309.04,
          "end": 313.24,
          "en": "So now if I add apples here, it flies in from the top, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 313.27,
          "end": 315.22,
          "en": "Of course we could set X to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 315.23,
          "end": 317.98,
          "en": "No, now to just have it come in from the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 317.98,
          "end": 322.05,
          "en": "So now if I add my apples here, it will just fly in from the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 322.06,
          "end": 328.27,
          "en": "So this is how you can also animate this, how you can animate the appearance with transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 328.27,
          "end": 333.31,
          "en": "Now you can also animate the disappearance, though, if we add a onClick listener because clicking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 333.31,
          "end": 339.76,
          "en": "should maybe remove that, we then add a discard function, then this is also pretty easy to achieve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 339.85,
          "end": 345.46,
          "en": "Let's add a function named discard here and now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 345.46,
          "end": 349.93,
          "en": "Let's say here we also bind this because I have to bind it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 349.93,
          "end": 352.81,
          "en": "And then as our argument that should be passed in the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 352.81,
          "end": 359.39,
          "en": "So the value of the item that should be removed, then we get that value here as an argument in this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 359.39,
          "end": 364.16,
          "en": "card and there we can update boxes to be equal to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 365.19,
          "end": 372.12,
          "en": "Boxes where we filter and where we check if the element is equal to value because then we don't want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 372.12,
          "end": 372.86,
          "en": "to keep it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 372.87,
          "end": 375.07,
          "en": "So we'll add an exclamation mark here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 375.09,
          "end": 377.28,
          "en": "Now with that, if we save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 378.86,
          "end": 382.74,
          "en": "And we add our apples and then our bananas.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 382.76,
          "end": 387.98,
          "en": "If I click apples now, you see the animation is inverted, is reverted, and it's removed.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
